ofile_images\\/1769430779845611520\\/lIgjSJGU_bigger.jpg"},"url":{"urlType":"DeepLink","url":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/xai"},"userLabelType":"BusinessLabel","userLabelDisplayType":"Badge"},"verified":false,"is_blue_verified":true,"verified_type":"Business"},"id":"biwQDeTYRKOX89cpqPwblsJOE","conversation_preview":[{"message":"do humans need aluminium in their bodies to survive","sender":"USER","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]},{"message":"Humans do not need aluminum in their bodies to survive. Aluminum is not considered an essential nutrient for human health, meaning there is no known biological function for aluminum in the human body. Here are some key points:\\nToxicity: While small amounts of aluminum are commonly ingested through food, water, and medications, high levels can be toxic. Aluminum toxicity can affect the nervous system, bones, and kidneys, particularly in individuals with impaired kidney function who cannot effectively excrete it.\\nExposure: Humans are exposed to aluminum through various sources like food (especially processed foods), drinking water, cookware, antiperspirants, and some medications like antacids. However, the body has mechanisms to manage small amounts of aluminum.\\nHealth Concerns: There\'s ongoing research into whether aluminum might play a role in diseases like Alzheimer\'s, though no direct causal link has been definitively established.\\nDietary Intake: Most people ingest aluminum daily in small quantities without adverse effects. The average intake is regulated by natural excretion processes in healthy individuals, mainly through the kidneys.\\nNutritional Role: Unlike elements like iron, calcium, or magnesium, which are vital for bodily functions, aluminum does not have a known beneficial role in human physiology.\\nIn summary, while aluminum is ubiquitous in the environment and our diet, it is not required for human survival or health. If you have concerns about aluminum exposure or its potential health impacts, consulting with a healthcare provider would be advisable.","sender":"AGENT","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]}],"destination":"destination_1","allowed_actions":[],"metadata":{"text":"Answer by Grok, expand to see full conversation"}}}},"destination_objects":{"destination_1":{"type":"browser","data":{"url_data":{"url":"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/i\\/grok\\/share\\/biwQDeTYRKOX89cpqPwblsJOE","vanity":"Grok"}}}},"components":["details_1"]}', 'type': 'STRING'}}, {'key': 'card_url', 'value': {'scribe_key': 'card_url', 'string_value': 'https://t.co/4LKDmrjEAL', 'type': 'STRING'}}], 'card_platform': {'platform': {'audience': {'name': 'production'}, 'device': {'name': 'Swift', 'version': '12'}}}, 'name': 'unified_card', 'url': 'https://t.co/4LKDmrjEAL', 'user_refs_results': []}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1883704591747084427'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1737948746000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '8', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 27 02:32:26 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1883691494613340357', 'display_text_range': [14, 95], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [{'display_url': 'x.com/i/grok/share/b…', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/i/grok/share/biwQDeTYRKOX89cpqPwblsJOE', 'url': 'https://t.co/4LKDmrjEAL', 'indices': [72, 95]}], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd humans shouldnt have aluminum in our bodies. grok agrees\n\nhttps://t.co/4LKDmrjEAL', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1883691494613340357', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'possibly_sensitive': Fals